From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: retry NPU re-init after L1 SER recovery

The L1 SER path stops the NPU, resets and restarts WFDMA, then hands the
NPU the rings again via __mt7996_npu_hw_init(), but ignores the result.
On an AN7581 W1700K the very first mailbox message after the DMA restart
(GET_WAIT_NPU_VERSION) has been seen to time out twice, roughly 0.25 s
after a successful npu_hw_stop. None of the NPU programming then runs (PCIe
port type, txrx offload rings, rxd/txd, rx_event, tx_done), while
mt76_npu_device_active() stays true, so NAPI keeps skipping the NPU-owned
queues and host TX waits for NPU tx-free that never arrives. The driver
reports "L1 SER recovery completed" with the data path dead; stations are
dropped for inactivity five minutes later. In the second occurrence an MCU
timeout followed ~290 s later and escalated into a full chip reset that does
not recover on this board either.

Retry the NPU re-init up to five times, 200 ms apart, which gives the NPU
firmware time to settle after the stop/restart. Steps before the failing
one are plain mailbox writes, so restarting from the version query is
safe. If it still fails, log an error rather than claiming success. The
error code is also added to the version-query warning so a mailbox timeout
(-ETIMEDOUT) can be told apart from an NPU status error (-EINVAL).

Signed-off-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
index 0cadeb2..e34c64d 100644
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2568,7 +2568,7 @@ void mt7996_mac_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	struct ieee80211_hw *hw;
 	struct mt7996_dev *dev;
 	struct mt7996_phy *phy;
-	int i;
+	int i, ret;
 
 	dev = container_of(work, struct mt7996_dev, reset_work);
 	hw = mt76_hw(dev);
@@ -2682,7 +2682,17 @@ void mt7996_mac_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 				     MT_INT_TX_RX_DONE_EXT);
 	}
 
-	__mt7996_npu_hw_init(dev);
+	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
+		if (i)
+			msleep(200);
+
+		ret = __mt7996_npu_hw_init(dev);
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(dev->mt76.dev,
+			"NPU re-init failed after L1 SER: %d\n", ret);
 
 	clear_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state);
 	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy)
diff --git a/mt7996/npu.c b/mt7996/npu.c
index 3a105f8..19b29e7 100644
--- a/mt7996/npu.c
+++ b/mt7996/npu.c
@@ -234,7 +234,8 @@ static int mt7996_npu_offload_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 	err = mt76_npu_get_msg(npu, 0, WLAN_FUNC_GET_WAIT_NPU_VERSION,
 			       &val, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (err) {
-		dev_warn(dev->mt76.dev, "failed getting NPU fw version\n");
+		dev_warn(dev->mt76.dev, "failed getting NPU fw version: %d\n",
+			 err);
 		return err;
 	}
 
